# Medicine POS Backend — Cursor Entry Point

> **All engineering rules live in `specs/CONSTITUTION.md`.**
> **All status lives in `specs/INDEX.md`.**
>
> This file is an entry point, not a rulebook. It restates no rules. If either of those files
> disagrees with this one, they win. Read `specs/CONSTITUTION.md` before your first edit.

## Where requirements live

Product requirements and the decisions log are in **Notion**, not in this repository. This
repo owns architecture, data model, API design, security and the module specs derived from
them. Cite a decision by number — `[D-73]`. If a requirement is missing or contradictory,
**ask**; do not invent one. Constitution Article III.

## The five gates

```
Gate 1  SPEC.md + CONTRACT.md   Gate 2  plan.md   Gate 3  tasks.md
Gate 4  implement               Gate 5  verify
```

**A task is ticked on a command that exits 0, never on intent.** No implementation may exist
in `crates/<module>/` before that module's `SPEC.md` exists.

## Commands

```bash
cargo xtask verify --lint        # structural, executes nothing
cargo xtask verify --module 07   # run one module's assertions
cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings
```

## How the gate reaches you

`crates/server/build.rs` runs the structural lint on every `cargo build`, `cargo check` and
`cargo test`, and `.githooks/pre-commit` catches the same violation at commit time.
`.cursor/hooks.json` adds the tick-time check where your runtime supports it.

Rules tagged `[CLAUDE]` in the constitution do not bind you — follow the `[ALL]` equivalent
stated alongside each one. In particular, run Gate 5 as a separate invocation that did not
implement the tasks, and never write against a crate API from recall: check the version in
`Cargo.toml` and read `cargo doc` or the installed source.
